# Python bytecode from the chart and art scripts.
__pycache__/

# Compiled output beside the source.
#
# Nothing should put it there and for a long time nothing did, so this is a
# backstop rather than a rule. `tsc -b` is build mode and emits whatever the
# config says; `build` and `typecheck` both used to force `--noEmit false` and
# scatter a .js beside every .ts in src/ and lab/. Vite resolves `.js` ahead of
# `.ts`, so the moment those exist, `vitest` and `npx vite-node lab/duel.ts`
# stop reading the source and start reading a stale copy of it — a balance
# measurement that silently answers about the code as it was at the last build.
# Both scripts now typecheck without emitting. This catches the next way in.
src/**/*.js
lab/**/*.js
# And the config itself, which is a .ts and was emitted as a .js at the root by
# the same runs. That one would have shadowed vite.config.ts outright.
/vite.config.js
